name: Homepage visual direction
description: Work-first editorial portfolio: Geist, monochrome + one mint accent, project cover art, light and dark themes
 type: design
---

Direction chosen by the owner (Oct 2026): a clean, work-first editorial portfolio — NOT a resume layout. Lead with a short statement hero, then "Selected work" as large cards with line-art covers (src/components/case-art.tsx), a featured first case study, smaller "AI builds" cards, a quiet impact band, About beside a compact expandable experience timeline, toolkit as plain text, and a contact card. Avoid framed rows, bullet-heavy blocks and tag soup on the homepage. Geist + Geist Mono, monochrome with mint used sparingly, generous whitespace, rounded cards with soft hover lift. Shared pieces live in src/components/site-frame.tsx (SiteHeader, SiteFooter with hatched wordmark, Cover, CaseShell, CASES); case studies use CaseShell (cover-art hero, meta row, hairline-separated sections via .case-frame, prev/next cards). Check every change in both themes and at phone width.
